{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StylebookTab",
  "tagName": "main",
  "$elements": [
    { "$ref": "../components/jx-action-button.json" },
    { "$ref": "../components/jx-icon.json" },
    { "$ref": "../components/jx-tab.json" },
    { "$ref": "../components/jx-tabs.json" }
  ],
  "style": {
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
    "color": "var(--jx-fg)",
    "background": "var(--jx-bg)",
    "padding": "var(--jx-space-6)",
    "minHeight": "100vh",
    "& > h1": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-lg)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)"
    },
    "& > h2": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "margin": "var(--jx-space-6) 0 var(--jx-space-3)"
    },
    "& > p": {
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)",
      "maxWidth": "60ch"
    },
    "& [slot=\"status\"]": {
      "borderRadius": "999px",
      "padding": "0 var(--jx-space-2)",
      "border": "1px solid var(--jx-border)",
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-xs)",
      "lineHeight": "var(--jx-leading-xs)",
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)"
    },
    "& [slot=\"icon\"]": {
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-muted)",
      "lineHeight": "1"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    { "tagName": "h1", "textContent": "jx-tab" },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "A tab is a string with a role, and three places a consumer may decorate it. Write label as an ATTRIBUTE — a property write does not reflect, and selectors read the attribute — and write it whenever anything is slotted: the label is the tab's accessible name, so slotted content never joins it, and a tab with no label falls back to naming itself from whatever was put inside."
    },
    { "tagName": "h2", "textContent": "States" },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "Selected, plain, dirty, closable, and a label longer than the tab is wide."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-tabs",
      "attributes": { "label": "Tab states", "selected": "one" },
      "children": [
        { "tagName": "jx-tab", "attributes": { "value": "one", "label": "Selected" } },
        { "tagName": "jx-tab", "attributes": { "value": "two", "label": "Plain" } },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "three", "label": "Unsaved", "dirty": "" }
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "four", "label": "Closable", "closable": "" }
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": {
            "value": "five",
            "label": "A label far longer than the tab it sits in",
            "closable": "",
            "dirty": ""
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    { "tagName": "h2", "textContent": "The three slots" },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "icon draws before the label, status and actions after it, and both land before the tab's own dirty dot and close button — so a consumer decorates a tab without re-implementing the tablist. There is deliberately no default slot: the tab's words are the label attribute, and unnamed content has nowhere to go."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "status is for a mark ABOUT the document (a draft pill, a count, a sync state) and actions is for a control (a pin, a lock). The difference is the click: a click on a mark is a click on the tab and selects it, and a click inside actions stops there, exactly as the close button's does."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-tabs",
      "attributes": { "label": "Slots", "selected": "post" },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "post", "label": "hello.md", "closable": "", "dirty": "" },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "span",
              "attributes": { "slot": "icon", "aria-hidden": "true" },
              "textContent": "↳"
            },
            { "tagName": "span", "attributes": { "slot": "status" }, "textContent": "Draft" },
            {
              "tagName": "jx-action-button",
              "attributes": { "slot": "actions" },
              "$props": {
                "icon": "eye",
                "size": "sm",
                "label": "Preview hello.md",
                "hint": "Preview",
                "tabindex": "0"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "about", "label": "about.md", "closable": "" },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "jx-icon",
              "attributes": { "slot": "icon", "aria-hidden": "true" },
              "$props": { "name": "file-text" }
            },
            { "tagName": "span", "attributes": { "slot": "status" }, "textContent": "Published" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "styles", "label": "main.css", "closable": "" }
        }
      ]
    },
    { "tagName": "h2", "textContent": "A control inside a tab" },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "A control in actions is in the tab order only while its tab is the current one — bind its tabindex the way the close button's is bound, or a strip of ten tabs becomes ten stops. jx-action-button takes tabindex as a property for exactly this. Enter and Space on it belong to the control; the arrows still move the strip's caret from wherever focus is."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-tabs",
      "attributes": { "label": "Roving caret", "selected": "current" },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "current", "label": "Current", "closable": "" },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "jx-action-button",
              "attributes": { "slot": "actions" },
              "$props": {
                "icon": "eye",
                "size": "sm",
                "label": "Preview Current",
                "hint": "Preview",
                "tabindex": "0"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "other", "label": "Other", "closable": "" },
          "children": [
            {
              "tagName": "jx-action-button",
              "attributes": { "slot": "actions" },
              "$props": {
                "icon": "eye",
                "size": "sm",
                "label": "Preview Other",
                "hint": "Preview",
                "tabindex": "-1"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    { "tagName": "h2", "textContent": "The close affordance" },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "It is a plain button with a jx-icon inside, never a nested kit button: a defined element that ships its own default slot would capture the host's slot distribution. The click stops at the button, so closing never also selects."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-tabs",
      "attributes": { "label": "Open documents", "selected": "index" },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "index", "label": "index.page.json", "closable": "" }
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-tab",
          "attributes": { "value": "about", "label": "about.page.json", "closable": "" }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
